# Every remainder this model can compute, beside what its filing established about the set it
# sits in. One row per computable remainder: the extent its stack declared, what its coupling
# search reported, and any spillover somebody else observed into it.
#
# A remainder needs a closed layer set
#   A remainder is only meaningful if the layer set is closed. `r = n - d` is a fact about one
#   layer, and the model then treats the stack as a set of independent quantizations. Two things
#   break that, and only one of them is about this document: nobody bounded the set, or a pair it
#   holds spills over. Count this relation by `standing` for how many remainders sit in a set
#   somebody established and how many in one nobody has asked about.
#
# The verdict is the assertion, not the answer
#   The verdict is computed for every remainder, and that is the assertion rather than the answer.
#   `unbounded` is the honest state for a filing written to argue about three layers, and it must
#   never fail anything. What must fail is a remainder that reaches the arithmetic without this
#   question having been put to it at all.
#
# `unbounded` is not a smaller `scoped`
#   epistemics/scopes.sqlc has the argument: `scoped` says somebody established what lies outside,
#   `unbounded` says nobody looked. Folding them would count a silence as a boundary.
-- layers/remainder.sqlc against pm:Stack/pm:scope, pm:couplings/pm:absent and entries/spillovers.sqlc.
SELECT r.filing, r.layer,
       sc.extent,
       cs.answer AS search,
       sp.observed_in AS spilled_from,
       CASE WHEN sp.observed_in IS NOT NULL THEN 'takes a spillover'::public.remainder_standing
            WHEN sc.extent = 'unbounded'    THEN 'nobody bounded the set'::public.remainder_standing
            WHEN cs.answer  = 'unmeasured'  THEN 'set bounded, pairs untested'::public.remainder_standing
            ELSE 'bounded and the pairs answered'::public.remainder_standing END AS standing
FROM      (
    :compose(layers/remainder.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(epistemics/scopes.sqlc)
) sc ON sc.filing = r.filing
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc)
) cs ON cs.filing = r.filing
LEFT JOIN ( SELECT DISTINCT borne_by, from_layer, observed_in FROM (
    :compose(entries/spillovers.sqlc)
) x ) sp ON sp.borne_by = r.filing AND sp.from_layer = r.layer
